Hi,

a new version of ypbind is available on
ftp://ftp.uni-paderborn.de/pub/linux/local/yp/ypbind-3.2.tar.gz.
Changes from 3.1: Fix a bug, which could cause ypbind to unregister itself
from the portmapper.

Note to Debian users: Your distribution contains the ported BSD ypbind, you
do not need to upgrade (but it should be safe).

Note to RedHat users: Your distribution uses the NYS-enabled libc, you do
not need to run ypbind.

Whatisit: ypbind finds the server for a NIS domain and provides this
information to NIS clients.

