Webroute is a simple web proxy that runs on Linux and perhaps some
other unixes (it has been reported to run on SunOs though I haven't
tested it yet). Its main advantage is that it is simple to use as
the only options are given on the command line, and that's all.
The new release handles better cached pages, so that it can make
the browser think that a page hasn't been modified to avoid a
modem connection when this is not necessary. It supports
connect/disconnect scripts which are useful for PPP.

I personnaly use it chained to squid to have an 'autoconnectable cache'.

It will be available on sunsite in a few days, and it is on:

  http://www-miaif.ibp.fr/willy/webroute/
or 
  ftp://aemiaif.ibp.fr/pub/webroute/


