- ----------------------------------------------------------
File:   uvfat-0.1.readme
Author: Michael Leodolter <Michael.Leodolter@univie.ac.at>
Date:   Mon Mar 31 14:33:20 MET DST 1997
- ----------------------------------------------------------

This is UVFAT Alpha 0.1 from UMSDOS 0.6.

        I copied linux/fs/umsdos --> linux/fs/uvfat
        and renamed all msdos-references to vfat-references.

What is UVFAT:

        UVFAT is as unix like filesystem on top of the VFAT (win95/nt
longnames) 
        filesystem. For additional information (owner, special
names,...) it
uses 
        a hidden file (-linux--.---).
        The main difference between UVFAT and UMSDOS is that UVFAT uses
the
long 
        longnames from VFAT if possible.
        Uvfat is 'umsdos' moved from 'msdos' to 'vfat':

                fat --- msdos --- umsdos
                     \- vfat  --- uvfat

       
How to get:
        To patch the kernel get:


<ftp://lab1.psy.univie.ac.at/pub/linux/uvfat/linux-2.0.28-uvfat-0.1.diff.gz>

or

<ftp://lab1.psy.univie.ac.at/pub/linux/uvfat/linux-2.1.38-uvfat-0.1.diff.gz>

        To patch umsdos_progs get:               


<ftp://lab1.psy.univie.ac.at/pub/linux/uvfat/umsdos_progs-0.9-uvfat-0.1.diff.gz>

Patch kernel:
        cd /usr/src
        zcat linux-2.0.28-uvfat-0.1.diff.gz | patch -p0 --      
	or
        zcat linux-2.1.38-uvfat-0.1.diff.gz | patch -p0 --      
        make any-config;
        make depend clean;
        make zImage modules modules_install

Patch umsdos_progs:
        cd /usr/local/src
        zcat umsdos_progs-0.9-uvfat-0.1.diff.gz | patch -p0 --
        make
        make install


New features:
        VFAT long-case-sensitive-filenames in UNIX and WinNT/95.

Moving from umsdos to uvfat:
        Mounting a umsdos-partition with uvfat will rename on
        lookup/readdir calls all umsdos-mangled files to vfat 
        long names if possible. 
        --linux-.--- still has mangled and long name as in umsdos.
        
Mangle:
        In uvfat all names get mangled. So the first instance of any
        case-file is in vfat & uvfat.
                
                touch Ma ma mb Mb
                /sbin/uvfatdosctl ls .
                .
                ..
                --linux-.---
                ma.{_1
                mb.{_3
                Ma
                Mb
                touch Ma1 ma1 mb1 Mb1
                /sbin/uvfatdosctl ls .
                .
                ..
                --linux-.---
                ma1.{_5
                Ma1
                mb1
                mb1.{_7
        

Moving from uvfat to umsdos:
        not yet - uvfat needs an ums-mount-option.
        
Syncing:
        Use umsdos_progs-0.9 + ufvat patch (uvfatsync,...).
        
Missing features:
        Still problems with short (8.3) filenames and mv.
        create: touch Na na Nb nb
        rename: mv -f Na nb
        result: ls *
                na nb
        This because of case insensitivity 
        of fat fs (any idea ??? M$ ???).

Warning:
        This is Alpha code!
                touch Na na Nb nb
                mv Na nb
        silently removes Nb (and Na as it should).

KernelVersion:
        Should work with 2.0.28/29 and some earlier.
        Should work with 2.1.38+.

Testing:
        Please send any test/bug-reports to
<michael.leodolter@univie.ac.at>.

Best regards,

        michael
