After a really long time, a new version of VICE, the Versatile Commodore
Emulator, has been released.  Most of the emulation code has been rewritten
from scratch to provide higher compatibility and better performance.

VICE is a multi-platform emulation system completely written in C; it
includes emulators for the Commodore 64, VIC20 and PET3032/4032/8032.  All
the emulators feature a complete Xaw-based GUI and a built-in monitor, and
support the most common Commodore emulator formats.

This version should run on most Unix system with X11R5 or later, at any
display depth.

The improvements over 0.11.0 include:

  - faster and more accurate emulation of the hardware;

  - hardware-level emulation of the Commodore 1541 floppy disk drive;

  - audio support for Linux, FreeBSD, SGI, HP-UX and Solaris;

  - complete Xaw-based GUI;

  - GNU configure script (easier compilation).

For more information, have a look at the official VICE homepage at

   http://www.tu-chemnitz.de/~fachat/vice/vice.html

The LSM entry follows.  Have fun!

Ettore.

