Elex
====

  Elex 0.1 is the first release of a new multi-language scanner
  generator package for Linux and other Unixen.  Elex is one of the
  few scanner generators that are not locked into one language.
  Currently C++ scanners are supported, with Java and Ada 95 support
  planned for the 1.0 release.  Support for other languages can be
  added without any modification to the Elex source.  See URL's below
  for more information.

License
=======

  Elex is released under the GNU Public License.

Requirements
============

  * Linux 1.x (untested) or 2.0.  Should run on other moderately
    POSIX-compliant Unix systems with GNU development tools.

  * GNU g++ 2.7.2.

  * GNU make 3.x.

  * Perl 5.001.

Download
========

  http://www.ozemail.com.au/~mpp/elex/elex.html
  (info and documentation)

  http://www.ozemail.com.au/~mpp/elex/elex-0.1.tar.gz
  (source)

  http://www.ozemail.com.au/~mpp/elex/elex-0.1.bin.tar.gz
  (i386 Linux ELF binary distribution)

Author
======

  Matthew Phillips <mpp@ozemail.com.au>



