This is to announce that unRAR 2.01 is available from
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/utils/compress/unrar-2.01.tar.gz
Please check your local sunsite mirror.

unRAR allows you to extract, view and test RAR archives created with
RAR version 1.50 and above (including 2.00 and 2.01).  It comes
with full source code and a prebuilt binary.

Just in case you don't know, RAR is a popular (and powerful) archiver
for DOS, Windows 95, OS/2 and some UNIX variants.  A Linux version
is also available from ftp://ftp.elf.stuba.sk/pub/pc/pack/ .

Because unRAR is freeware (as opposed to the RAR archiver, which
is shareware), it is suitable for inclusion into a Linux distribution.

