DFM - The Desktop-File-Manager for X11
======================================

Version alpha-9

DFM is a desktopmanager for linux and other UNIX-OS. Files are shown
as icons and every folder has it's own window. The desktopbackground
is a special folder in the homedirectory.

The idea is to write a filemanager like the OS/2 WPS.

Here are the current features:

* icons may have any size and position
* show XVPICS as icons
* every file has it's own shell-command (activated by double click or
  drop on the icon)
* save icon and window info
* every DFM-window has it's own background
* copy, move, link, delete, ...
* detail view (without icons)
* structure view
* arrange icons in a grid
* iconname to cutbuffer (paste to xterm, ...)
* "Constant position" icons that cannot be moved (or arranged)
* create own XVPICS (extern)
* easy adding new programs to the desktop
* sort icons
* update automatically
* ...

New since alpha-4
* config script
* create own XVPICS (extern)
* easy adding new programs to the desktop
* IRIX support
* SunOS support
* doesn't need the "*_mask.xpm" files any more
* icons on the desktop are now childs of the rootwindow :-)
* speed up
* The context of the windowmanager is now available by first pressing
  the middle mouse key.
* save ".dfminfo" with libgz (factor 6-10)
* new slider outfit
* checkbutton for the caching of windows
  (Disable caching for Enlightenment or if you have less memory)
* Hide ".*" files
* able to change the font of the icons
* update all 40 sec
* bugfixes

You need

   c-compiler, xforms, libXpm, libXext, X11, 16MB and a windowmanager

Available from:
http://www-c.informatik.uni-hannover.de/~kaiser/dfm/dfm.html ca. 150 KByte

Have fun and keep care: NO WARRANTY

You may distribute under the terms of the GNU General Public License
as specified in the COPYING file.

