Description
===========

Red Hat Motif 2.0.1 is the full OSF/Motif development system. Red Hat Motif
will turn your Linux PC into a Motif development workstation. This release
is ported specifically for use with the new X11R6 (XFree86 3.2) version of
the XWindow system. 

For developers, Motif 2.0.1 makes creation of software applications and
custom widgets simple. The many toolkit enhancements, new widgets, and UIL
improvements provide uncomplicated application portability across a variety
of platforms. 

New for this edition is the KL Group's XRT Professional Developer's Suite 
(PDS), a package of market-leading widgets and utilities for professional 
Motif developers.  The PDS has a retail value of $5,000, but is provided
at no extra cost to Red Hat Motif customers.

For end users, Red Hat Motif 2.0.1 improves their interface performance.
The virtual screen support unclutters their workspace by providing alternate
locations for chosen windows, while providing greater consistency with PC
environments. 


Features
========

 o An extensibility framework to ease application and widget development.
   Support for desktop infrastructures such as virtual window management
   and workspace management.

 o Numerous toolkit enhancements including a Uniform Transfer Model (UTM)
   for simplified data transfer. 

 o Convergence with PC styles including seven new widgets.

 o UIL improvements which include 64-bit support, platform independent uid
   files and support of extensibility features.

 o A common user interface across a wide range of applications and platforms.
   Easy-to-use PC windowing-style interactive behavior, providing users with
   rapid skill transfer.

 o Distinctive 3-D beveled user interface elements.

 o A single, stable, widely available application programming interface
   (API) allowing application developers to "write it once" for many
   platforms.

 o A superior set of tools offering high developer productivity in
   establishing a consistent look and feel.

 o Internationalization, easing access to worldwide markets.

 o Hardware independence for scalability across all types of operating and
   file systems. 

 o Network transparency based on the XWindow system.


Red Hat Motif includes:
