DIALMON - A DIALD MONITOR
- -------   ---------------

DIALMON is a monitor daemon which complements the diald daemon, and
allows client programs on other machines to display the current state
of diald (down, connected, etc.), to bring the link up and, optionally,
to take the link down. I have included clients which run on WfWG3.11
(with TCP/IP), on Win95/NT, and Linux/X.

The sources, plus the Windows executable, have been uploaded to
sunsite.unc.edu, and should appear in /pub/Linux/system/daemons as
dialmon-0.1.tgz and dialmon-0.1.lsm in due course..

The LSM is:

- ----------------
Begin3
Title:          dialmon-0.2
Version:        30-May-97
Entered-date:   30-May-97
Description:    Dialmon is a monitor daemon for diald which allows
		clients on remote machines to display the current
		status of diald, to bring the link up and, optionally,
		to take the link down. Clients for Linux (tcl/tk),
		Win31 and Win95/NT are included.
Keywords:       diald windows
Author:         mike@quaking.demon.co.uk
Maintained-by:  mike@quaking.demon.co.uk
Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pup/Linux/system/daemons
		151kB dialmon-0.1.tgz
		1kB   dialmon-0.1.lsm
Alternate-site: http://www.quaking.demon.co.uk/dialmon.html
Original-site:  
Platforms:      WfWG3.11+TCP/IP, Win95, Linux/X
Copying-policy: GPL
End
- ----------------

This is actually the third version. I would be grateful if dialmon could
be retrieved, be preference, from sunsite (or from a mirror) rather than
the http server.

All comments, suggestions, and, of course, bug reports, welcome to
mike@quaking.demon.co.uk

Have fun.


