Unix Cockpit 2.0 available for Linux-2.0

I'm happy to announce the release of the Unix Cockpit 2.0 (UC). Binaries for
AIX, FreeBSD, HP-UX, Irix, Linux, Dec OSF1, Reliant/Sinix, Solaris and SunOS
are available on http://www.UniX11.com (http://208.192.103.13).

Unix Cockpit is a nifty Unix/X11 file manager that combines convenience with 
power. File browsers, a directory tree, custom menus and your standard 
command shell are smoothly integrated into one highly customizable, 
multi-window productivity tool of a kind long missed on Unix systems. 
Everything from mouse-based drag and drop to fast keyboard operations is 
supported.

If you like XTree Gold or the Norton Commander, or if you're fed up with 
point-click-curse interfaces, or if you want to extend the power of the 
command line, this program is for you. UC is easy to learn, and also has
full context sensitive help and an online tutorial built-in. Everything
is contained in a single small executable that runs efficiently even on
older Unix machines. 

Unix Cockpit 2.0 is uncrippled shareware that is fully functional even
if not registered, so you can test it to your heart's desire. Screenshots
and binaries can be downloaded via WWW from http://www.UniX11.com and 
via anonymous ftp from ftp.uu.net, directory /vendor/UniX11.

Cheers,
