Caldera's OpenLinux Standard (http://www.caldera.com) has just been
reviewed by InfoWorld Magazine. It is a stellar review by Nicholas
Petreley. The article is printed in the May 26, 1997 issue on page 100
and can be found in the mags website at http://www.infoworld.com.

Nicholas Petreley writes:

"Caldera's OpenLinux Standard 1.1 - the company's system for
distributing Linux - keeps getting better and better."

"Linux purists will probably prefer Red Hat, but everyone else should
find Caldera OpenLinux the best Linux distribution available."

"The FastTrack server, coupled with the Linux high-performance kernal,
makes Caldera OpenLinux an unbeatable value as a Web Server.  This is
true even for Windows shops, bacause Caldera includes native Windows
file and print services. That means you can run the product as the Web
server and use Windows clients for Web authoring and administration."

"The inclusion of DOS and the Netscape server represents a bold move
made by Caldera to mainstream Linux. So far it looks like an effort well
spent."



