Version 1.1 of qps is now available.

qps is a process status monitor, an X11 version of top or ps that displays
processes in a window and lets you sort and manipulate them easily.

Major differences from version 1.0 are:

o Posix.1b realtime control:  Want to give your X server or mpeg player
  realtime priority, just to see what happens?  Now it's easy.
o Per-process window of TCP/UDP sockets (like netstat, but for each process)
o User interface facelift, including a load graph which can be displayed in
  the icon when iconified
o Some new fields added
o WCHAN is displayed in symbolic form
o Old bugs fixed, new bugs added

Qps should compile on any platform (intel, alpha, sparc etc) running Linux
2.0.x.  A binary for x86 is included.

The Qt library version 1.1 or later is required.  It can be downloaded from
ftp://ftp.troll.no or http://www.troll.no

Begin3
Title:          qps - visual process status monitor
Version:        1.1
Entered-date:	19MAY97
Description:    An X11 based process status monitor, like top(1) but based on
                the Qt toolkit, listing the processes in a periodically
                updated window. Processes can be reniced and have signals
                sent to them. Supports Posix.1b realtime scheduling.
                Qt 1.1 or later is required.
