I'd like to invite all of you to the 10th workshop of the OTA Linux SIG
on Saturday, June 7th. The OTA Linux Special Interest Group (Linux SIG) 
is a bridge between the fast evolving Linux Internet activity and the 
Belgian Linux users.


The program:
- ------------

09:15 doors open, welcome and coffee

09:45 - 10:45
Example of an Intranet (based on Linux) in a clinical environment.

By Willy Wittesaele - UZA

Within a clinic a lot of reports , results , letters etc... are generated.
An INTRANET is one possibility to offer them to the users. The following 
topics will be discussed : Apache WWW server , conversion of Xbase files 
to HTML with Codebase , connectivity with Novell servers , conversion of 
WordPerfect files to HTML etc... 

coffee-break
10:45 - 11:15

11:15 - 12:15
Linux, a linchpin to the Generale.

By Jan Mevis - Generale

Linux has  a  major operational role in the LAN of the Generale.
It also serves as a test bed for new applications with unknown - or
undocumented - network behavior. Since we mainly use Macintoshes as
user desktops, we're also interested in MkLinux on Apple Macintoshes.


Location:
- ---------
VUB (Vrije Universiteit Brussel) - Jette Faculty of Medicine
Building A - 1st floor - "informaticalokaal"
Laarbeeklaan 103, B-1090 Brussels


Participation fee:
- ------------------

350,- BEF for OTA members, 750,- BEF for non-members at entrance.


For more information about the OTA Linux SIG, please see

        http://www.ota.be/

or mail me (the OTA Linux SIG co-ordinator)

        Frederik.Cheeseman@ping.be

Again, looking forward to the workshop and hoping to see you there.

Best Regards

Frederik Cheeseman


