                  Release of ypserv 1.2.0
                  =======================

Version 1.2.0 of an YP (NIS version 2) Server for Linux is released.
It also runs under SunOS 4.1.x, Solaris 2.x, AIX, HP-UX, IRIX, Ultrix 
and OSF1 (alpha).

The programs are needed to turn your workstation in a NIS server. 
It contains ypserv, ypxfr, rpc.ypxfrd, rpc.yppasswdd, yppush, ypinit, 
revnetgroup, makedbm and /var/yp/Makefile.

This is NOT an NIS+ (NIS version 3) Server !

ypserv 1.2.0 is available under the GNU General Public License.

If you use a ypserv version prior to 1.1.6, you should upgrade. Old 
versions of ypserv have security problems and creates corrupted maps 
and send wrong timestamps to your NIS slaves. 


What's new since 1.1.7 ?
- ------------------------

 * ypserv will cache the file handles for faster database lookups

 * rpc.yppasswdd from yppasswd-0.10 is now included. This version has a 
   better shadow support then yppasswd-0.9.
 
 * optional installation of yppasswd

 * little changes to make the life harder for hackers

 * a lot of more changes.


You could get the latest version from:

http://www-vt.uni-paderborn.de/~kukuk/linux/
ftp://wauug.erols.com/pub/net/nis
ftp://ftp.lysator.liu.se/pub/NYS/server

