ASR Announces First Graphical System to Fully Integrate with
the Internet


RIPmaster 2.0 for Linux Offers Lightning Fast Graphical
Display along with Unlimited Flexibility


WEST LINN, OREGON (May 20, 1997) -- Advanced Systems
Research today announced release of the first online
graphical system to fully and seamlessly integrate with the
Internet while providing the fastest and most robust online
graphics protocol available. RIPmaster 2.0 for Linux creates
a stunning new type of technology for open system design of
online systems.

Designed from the ground up to be completely transparent to
the Internet, RIPmaster 2.0 for Linux is a graphically based
system using the extensive RIPscrip(tm) 3.0 protocol.  This
fully configurable design allows for the creation of
stunning graphics and multimedia systems.

"With RIPmaster 2.0, one can create any type of look and
operation imaginable. There are virtually no limits, except
one's own imagination, to what can be created and achieved.
Best of all, is the speed of transmission and display of the
graphics. The system actually gets faster as the caller uses
it," said Alan McNamee, President of Advanced Systems
Research.

Since RIPmaster 2.0 for Linux is a network based system,
there is also virtually no limit to the number of
simultaneous users.  RIPmaster boasts the FASTEST graphics
protocol and uses FAR less bandwidth than a comparable web
site.  RIPmaster is a persistent streaming TCP connection
which means that menu loads are instantaneous without
network lag or reconnection.  All resources that are
transferred to the client system are sent using ZLIB
compression, the same compression used in the new PNG image
format.  This automatic compression transfer further reduces
the amount of time required to navigate the online system.

RIPmaster runs under Linux on any supported hardware
platform, including the DEC Alpha workstation.  This open
platform architecture allows the system operator to select
from a wide variety of application development tools and
thousands of free and commercial packages -- all of which
can be integrated seamlessly into the RIPmaster 2.0 system.
Linux also allows one to integrate and run DOS applications
and DOOR programs in the online environment and for
connections to Novell, Appletalk, Windows and other
networks.  It supports a wide range of software, including
Emacs and TCP/IP networking (including SLIP/PPP/ISDN).
Independent benchmark tests on 80486 Linux systems have
found them comparable with mid-range workstations from Sun
and Digital.

"RIPmaster 2.0 operates transparently of Linux and requires
very little, if any, knowledge of Linux itself.  Since
RIPmaster was designed to be installed and operated 100%
remotely, it can be setup and operated from any site running
Linux in the world without the need for administrative
access to the host system.  RIPmaster is a perfect fit for
an ISP's cohab operation," said McNamee.

A 100% functional demonstration version of RIPmaster 2.0 for
Linux that allows for the design and creation of a working
system is available for FREE. The registered version, which
includes a registration key that disables the demonstration
message that appears during logon and a fully registered and
redistributable DOS and Windows client software (RIPterm(tm) and
RIPtel(tm)) is available for $599.95.

The RIPmaster demo system, RIPtel(tm) 3.0.2, and additional
tools can be download from http://www.telegrafix.com/asr.

Advanced Systems Research (ASR) which is headquartered in
West Linn, Oregon creates and designs custom databases,
programs and applications for online systems.


###

RIPmaster 2.0 for Linux Partial Feature List


There are hundreds of features present in RIPmaster 2.0,
here is just a few of them:

 - Automatic system resource updating
 - Built-in CompuServe type Jump Word command system
 - Built-in Global Help System
 - Built-in Global Commands System
 - Realtime Menu Command Editor
 - Built-in user inactivity application execution
 - Built-in WAV file playback for LOGON, WAITING MAIL, LOGOFF,
   RESTRICTED ACCESS, JUMP WORD ACTIVATION and individual Unix
   commands or RIPmaster commands.
 - Built-in Menu Caching System
 - Enhanced support for ALL Unix commands and applications.
 - Built-in and highly configurable file reader with page
   forward, reverse, D/L, search.  Look and feel are specified
   by the sysop.
 - Displays can be individually made to be any size and location
   on the screen or just as a WINDOW over the current menu.
 - WAV file playback support for ANY Unix or RIPmaster command.
 - Built in Transit resource transferring for menu loads and any
   Unix commands or applications.
 - Support for multiple languages.
 - Configurable user registration system.
 - Support for WEB page port execution.
 - TBBS style privilege and authorization flags.
 - Multiple server and Local and Wide area Network support.
 - Built-in firewall system.
 - Individual and Group account access.
 - Access log tracking, includes hostname tracking.
 - Dayfile log tracking.
 - New user registrations sent to sysop by e-mail.
 - WWW, Telnet, Gopher, News, Mail and FTP access.
 - Transmitted in-line compressed resource extraction.
 - 56-bit salted password encryption.
 - Popup picklist of last 10 operations.

