End


In more detail:


MixSLab
- -------

A suite of applications for direct to disk digital audio recording, mixing and
signal manipulation. MixSLab itself is a launchpad for the remaining 4 
applications. The applications themselves may consists of several programmes
and/or processes.

StudioSLab:
- -----------

Maximum configuration: (see release notes for more realistic operational
limitations)

64 Tracks.
16 Send/Return busses (8 pre fader, 8 post fader).
4 Stereo busses.
2 audio devices, 44.1kHz, 16 bit stereo, provides quadraphonic/auxilliary mix.

Each Track:
        Input device select.
        Input gain.
        PreSends, with bus selection.
        Dynamic Digital Filter (DDF), 5 algorithms with optional bypass:
                EQ: HI Gain, LO Gain.
                EQ: HI Cutoff and Gain, LO Cutoff and Gain.
                EQ: HI Cutoff/Gain/Feedback, LO Cutoff/Gain/Feedback.
                BandPass: gain, frequency and Q controls.
                Notch: gain, frequency and Q controls.
        PostSends, with bus selection.
        Stereo panning.
        Mute.
        Solo.
        Boost (3 dB signal gain).
        Stereo Bus Selection.
        Volume Fader.
        Track notes scratchpad.

16 Return Busses:
        Volume control, up to +3dB return signal.
        Left, Right controls.
        Output Device Selection Any of the 8 available audio devices.
        Effects attachments.

4 Stereo Busses:
        Volume pot,
        Left, Right fader controls.

VU Meters:
        16 independant fully configurable VUs.
        Simultaneous peak and RMS display.
        Sources: input L/R, output L/R, any track.

Master Controls:
        MasterVolume.
        Master Left, Right controls.
        Dynamic Digital Filter per L/R.

MicroMix:
        OSS/Free options controller, one per audioDev.



EffectSLab:
- -----------

This is a set of DSP algorithms running as modules, with the "EffectSLab"
being a 19 inch rack window. The Following algorithms are available now:

    Echo    - configurable delay, decay and feedback.
    Reverb    - Spread, depth and feedback - hall/room type effect.
    Streverb- Spread, depth and feedback - Stereo hall/room type effect.
    Streverb2    - Spread, depth and feedback - Stereo hall/room alternate algo.
Chorus    - configurable speed and breadth.
    stChorus- Stereo chorus, configurable speed and breadth.
    stNewAPIChorus- Same as above, but uses alternative API definitions.
    Flanger    - Speed and breadth.
    Phaser    - Speed, depth, feedback, Max and Q parameters.
    MultiTap- Spread, depth and feedback. Delay line with 4 taps.
    Spacial    - The MultiTap algo, 4 tap delay line, with each tap at a
            configurable delay and level.
    Spacial2- Stereo MultiTap algo, 4 tap delay line, with each tap at a
            configurable delay and level, taps 1 and 3 left, 2 and 4 right.
    Rotary    - Stereo rotary speaker algorithm.
    Overotary    - Stereo rotary speaker with vanzeggelaars valve overdrive
                algorithm mixed in for full rotary speaker simulation.
    Limitor    - Limit, Factor. Simple excess signal compression.
    Limitor2    - Sensitivity/Threshold/Attack, Sensitivity/Threshold/Decay
            Level/Factor params, gated limitor algorithm.
    NoiseGate    - Sensitivity/Threshold/Attack, Sensitivity/Threshold/Decay
                gating algorithm.
    Compressor    - Sensitivity/Threshold/Attack, Sensitivity/Threshold/Decay
                and signal Level params.
    Distortion    - Speaker distortion algorithm, very noisy.
    OverDrive    - VanZeggelaars valve overdrive, 2 algorithms of creamy valve
                distortion and one transitor algo with control over input bias
                and gain.
    BlueValve    - VanZeggelaars creamy valve overdrive, with 3 bands of
                active EQ.
    BlueValveIt    - Bluevalve with external user interface.
    Equalizer    - 8 band equalizer, with SLab user interface.
    Stereographic    - 8 band stereo graphic equalizer with spectral analyser.

All effects use the optional user interface definitions. Undocumented APIs are
provided for creation of new effects. Source code of the echo, flanger and
stereo chorus are provided, however, as examples using the API. Most of the
effects are mono, but stereo support is provided in the APIs via ability to
register for multiple busses (see source for stereo chorus). There are hooks
available to allow the effects code itself to generate the values displayed
in the GUI. This allows the effect to indicate literal values and parameter
units in the display.

The StereoGraphic actually uses its own user interface, as an exception to the
rule (all the rest use the MixSLab Effects Interface). The effect has
an 8 band slider set for left and right, plus an imported VU meter for the
spectral analysis. The API provides for the capacity to allow the effect to 
only link into the data stream for a given bus, but deline to use the GUI. To
programme with this method, do not add any controllers during effect init. The
engine will interupt the effect (SIGUSR1) when data is available on the bus,
allowing asynchronous notification of user data availability. It is a bit of
a CPU pig, but it is running a serious set of filters per sample.

In addition, the mixing engine can introduce vinyl scratch, crosstalk and 
wow/flutter for analogue distortion reproductions, to reduce clinical 
quality of digital audio.

WaveSLab:
- ---------

Visual wave/sample editor, operates on multiple tracks or with multiple
waveSLabs.  Tools will operate on tracks or selections, with tooling for:

        normalisation
        copy
        merge
        gain
        reverse
        fade
        erase

Interface implements drag and drop operations. There are no "undo" options,
and so edits are destructive. Full status bars and floating menus. Implements
sample zooming and on-line magnification rotary controls for sample inspection,
and scrolling mechanisms.



TapeSLab:
- ---------

Tape Controls:

        Stop, Play, Forward, Rewind, SessionRecord, SessionPlay.
        SearchForward, SearchReverse, Pause, Record/Pause.

Track control menus.

MixDown Session Recording facilities - continuous controller automation.

8 memory locations for tape positioning.

Full LCD display.

SMPTE tape counters 24, 25 and 30 fps display (29.97 will also be implemented).

NOTES
- -----

If you only have a single soundblaster card, which is very usual, this
application will not provide very good results. There will be no duplex 
support, so recording whilst mixing will not be possible. You will either
need a duplex soundcard, or two soundcards, both configurations are supported.

