For immediate Release
BlackMail 0.24
License: GPL/Public Domain


Announcing BlackMail 0.24.  This is a bug-fix release over the previous
release, which was made public on April 29th.  Thanks to all the bug
testers and everyone who joined the mailing list, I was able to
eradicate the bugs quickly and offer this update.

BlackMail is a mailer proxy that wraps around your existing mailer
(preferrably smail) and provides protection against spammers, mail
forwarding, and the like.

For those of you on comp.os.smail looking for a proxy, you may want to
look into this.  This is a tested product, and works very well.  I am
interested in getting this code incorporated into SMAIL, so if you are
interested in doing this task, please feel free.

You can download blackmail from ftp.bitgate.com:/pub/blackmail.  Please
join the Lunchmeat Mailing List by writing a message to
majordomo@northwest.com, with "subscribe lunchmeat-ml" in the body of
the message.  You can also view the web page at
http://www.bitgate.com/spam/.

TOGETHER WE CAN FIGHT INTERNET SPAM!

Thank you for your time!  I look forward to positive responses.

- -- Ken Hollis


