The Linux Remote-Boot mini-HOWTO has been completely updated.
The latest version (with links to downloadable software) can be 
found at

	http://cuiwww.unige.ch/~mvuilleu/configsc1/config.html

and soon on your favorite Sunsite mirror.

It describes how to build a very robust server-based configuration
for a cluster of PC, allowing the user to choose at boot time
between Linux, DOS/Windows 3.1 or Windows 95. Client PC are
cleaned at each boot, thus offering the best safety to the users
of risky environments such as student labs.

