This is release 0.3 of cs, a program which is similar to the commercial
cscope(1).  cs indexes C sources and allows interactive queries using the
generated index.

At this stage, cs is only suitable for projects <100,000 lines of code.
The following changes were made since version 0.2:

o  Various bug fixes
o  The check for POSIX naming violations is back, but not yet finished
o  More consistent keyboard control
o  Much faster
o  Builds and works on SunOS 4.1.2 and FreeBSD, too

cs should work on any system which supports the following:

o  POSIX
o  ANSI C
o  SYSV curses library

URL: ftp://cantor.informatik.rwth-aachen.de/pub/unix/cs-0.3.tar.gz

Michael




