I have created a British spelling version of the dictionary file
(/usr/dict/words) included with most Linux distributions.  It is
similar to the normal version, but has US spellings in the list
replaced with their British equivalents.  So, Linux users in the UK,
Australia, etc. can now have a words file with local spellings. I have
also prepared RPM packages of the ispell spell checker built against
this British words list, as well as ispell's own British dictionary.

At present, the list is rather a quick hack. It almost certainly
contains US spelt words that I've missed, and lacks some words which
should be there (I know of several already).

I have the words list as a tar archive, with similar layout to that of
the normal US words list. I addition, I have made RPM packages of the
words list, for users of Red Hat Linux, or other RPM users. To go with
these are RPMs of the ispell spell checker package, which are built
with ispell's British dictionary joined with the British words list.

The relevant files are:

linux.words.2.british.tar.gz (size 138451)
	The words list itself.
linux.words.2.british.src.tar.gz (size 143082)
	The US words list with information and Makefile for the
	conversion to British.
words-2-3british.i386.rpm (size 139952)
	Drop in British replacement for Red Hat's words-2-3 RPM
	on i386 architecture.
words-2-3british.src.rpm (size 140175)
	Source RPM for above.
ispell-3.1.20-3british.i386.rpm (size 438596)
	Drop in British replacement for Red Hat's ispell RPM.
ispell-3.1.20-3british.src.rpm (size 687570)
	Source RPM for above.

The files are available from two FTP sites, presently:

nyquist.ecs.soton.ac.uk (thanks to Martin Ebourne)
	Tar archives under /pub/linux, i386 RPMs under
/pub/redhat/RPMS/i386, source RPMs under /pub/redhat/SRPMS.

samba.anu.edu.au (thanks to Andrew Tridgell)
	Tar archives under /pub/linux/dict, i386 RPMs under
/pub/linux/dict/RPMS-lorax, source RPMs under
/pub/linux/dict/SRPMS-lorax. This site is presently missing the
"words" RPMs. With luck they will be added shortly.

For the moment please direct all comments regarding the package to
	british-words%brucehall20@bohm.anu.edu.au
** This addresses is likely to be invalid by the end of 1997 or
possibly earlier.

If missing, or incorrect words are reported, I will attempt to fix the
problem and distribute updated lists.

