The June meeting of the Cincinnati Linux Users Group will be 
on Saturday June 7 at 10:30 a.m..  The location will be:

Compuware Branch Office
West Lake Center
4555 Lakeforest Dr., Suite 420
Blue Ash, OH

Compuware is located in Blue Ash near the intersection of Reed
Hartman Highway and Glendale Milford Road.  The office building
is behind Bennigan's and across the street from Embassy Suites.
The meeting will be in Suite 420 on the fourth floor.

See a map at the following URL:

http://www.vicinity.com/yt.hm?FAM=mapblast&CMD=GEO&SEC=find&IC=0%3A0%3A5&IC%3A=Compuware&AD2=4555+Lakeforest+Dr&AD3=Cincinnati%2C+OH+45242

Thanks to Jim Weirich for setting this up.

Agenda for June Meeting

The primary purpose of the June meeting will be to collect dues for
membership and to discuss progress in setting up the group.  We will 
also discuss areas where we need help.  Below is the agenda for the 
meeting.

1. Status of the Group
2. Status of the Web Site
3. Programs for Next Few Meetings
4. Open Forum

Ideas for Programs

Jeff Gilton will be coordinating programs for the monthly meetings.  
He is looking for ideas and for volunteers.  Anyone with ideas can 
send them to him at jeffg@castlec.com or bring them to the meeting.

Most important, we need volunteers for the next few meetings.  Send 
this information to Jeff too.

Web Site

OneNet has agreed to donate a corporate Web site for use by the
Cincinnati Linux Users Group.  In addition to an actual Web site, 
OneNet has software for an email list server.

We plan to begin by setting up a simple Web site and an email list.  
The email list will provide a forum for Linux users to ask questions. 
It will also be used as one method for posting information about the
group.

Jim Weirich will be heading up the development of our Web site.  We 
will discuss that at the June meeting too.  Anyone who is interested
should come to the meeting or contact Jim directly at jweirich@one.net.

Joining the Cincinnati PC Users Group

To be a member of the Cincinnati Linux Users Group, a Special Interest
Group of the Cincinnati PC Users Group, you must be a member of the
Cincinnati PC Users Group.  Normal membership dues for the Cincinnati 
PC Users Group is $35 per family.  For a limited time, a discounted 
dues price of $25 per family will be accepted for anyone joining the
Cincinnati Linux Users Group.

We will be accepting applications at the June meeting.  Anyone not 
able to attend the meeting can send an application to:

Jeff Gilton
8600 Swigert Road
Loveland, OH 45140

An application is attached.

Fill out the application but send it to the address above along with a 
check for $25.  (The form was copied from the CPCUG flyer.  It says 
$35 because that is the normal price.  Only $25 is required if you 
join by the June meeting.)  

I will forward applications to the Cincinnati PC Users Group.  By
sending applications to me, I will make sure the discounted price 
will be accepted.

The discounted price is good through the June 7 meeting.  Anyone 
who wants to join by mail should send their application to me 
before that meeting.

What is our Name?

As you may have noticed, I am still referring to us as the Cincinnati
Linux Users Group.  We will be working with the Cincinnati PC Users
Group to determine whether that is acceptable.  We have been added 
to some national lists of Linux Users Groups and I would like to keep 
a separate name but there may be restrictions placed on us by the 
parent organization.  I hope to have this resolved by the June meeting.

