Hello all!

After a long wait, I am releasing XBanner 1.31 - mainly a maintenance
release for XBanner 1.3, but some new features are also included.

XBanner is a nice little program whose sole purpose is to help you make
your XDM login screen look a lot better. XBanner is considered to be
'postcardware' - if you like it, please send me a postcard of the area
where you live. Otherwise it is free software under the terms of the GPL.

Home page: http://physics.fullerton.edu/XBanner/
Main FTP:  ftp://physics.fullerton.edu/pub/Linux/XBanner/

(A lot of mirror sites exist for the WWW page as well as the ftp area)

RedHat and Debian users will find a RedHat rpm package file and a Debian
deb package file (RedHat 4.1, Debian 2.0 - when it comes out). XBanner is
a part of the RedHat and Debian distributions so future releases will
already contain this release.

(Note - the .RPM is not ready yet, expect separate announcement).

Here's a short summary of what's changed in XBanner 1.31:

* Reverse color cycling direction every few steps (for text / background
  separately).
* Handle redrawing of uncovered areas as a feature (no longer a patch).
* Bug fixes for some weird situations that have been reported.
In general this is a maintenance release.

I'd like to thank two people - Chris Y. <yeo@hssktn3.sk.sympatico.ca> and
Joey Hess <joey@kite.ml.org> for creating the RedHat and Debian packages.
Their help and support proved again to be invaluable.

