SmallEiffel -0.86 is on sunsite.unc.edu and (soon) on
tsx-11.mit.edu.  Look for "se-0.86.tar.gz" on those sites.

The present version incorporates several bug fixes and a few new
features.

SmallEiffel is a GPL implementation of Eiffel, a full-featured
object-oriented programming language.

Eiffel delivers smooth and effortless interaction of multiple
inheritance, templates, and aggregation, brought about by the
careful and workmanlike plan of this language.

This brings the skilled designer unparalleled flexibility and
freedom in constructing reuseable class libraries.

Eiffel is available for multiple platforms in a variety of
commercial, shareware, and freeware implementations.  SmallEiffel is
the only actively  maintained free implementation of Eiffel for
Linux.

SmallEiffel still lacks a number of features found in the some other
implementations.  For example: garbage collection, exceptions, an
Integrated Development Environment, or even a full suite of support
tools.  These things will no doubt be built, in time.

However, SmallEiffel is free.

Also, it offers good portability because it requires no proprietary
runtime library.  Garbage collection (Boehm-Demers-Weiser, from
parcftp.xerox.com://pub/gc) may be installed as an add-on, following
instructions found in the distribution.

