ESEM Gruenau GmbH announces the first public release of ESEMfax.
  ESEMfax lets you share a faxmodem which is connected to a unix-box over
  a local network.

WHAT IS IT
ESEMfax is a mgetty+sendfax-frontend which runs under ms-windoze(3.11/95/nt).
you can send a fax to a linux-box where it gets handled via sendfax. on the
linux-side, you need a tiny daemon which is included in this distribution.
(when i refer to linux, i should better say: any unix that mgetty runs on.
i've only tested it under linux, but to my knowledge, there is no
linux-specific code inside).

WHERE TO GET IT
from http://www.esem.com/distri/esfa101u.zip 
you may also get it by mime- or uuencoded email, just drop me a line
(nittka@esem.com)
if people are interested, i'll perhaps upload it to where mgetty lives,
or something.

CHANGES
those who used the beta-versions might want to
know what has changed since then:
- - bugfixes all over the place :) in the beta version i had problems with
  garbled data on fast machines. this is fixed. esemfax runs pretty
  stable now.
- - faxq and faxwatch32 are new.


for more information, see http://www.esem.com/esemfax.html

