MPAS (Multi-Platform Access System) Software provides a convenient 
alternative to Linux resource management.  MPAS is a client-based
interface designed to work with ANY server using the SMB resource
sharing protocol. MPAS gives the system administrator quick and
efficient control over the handling and manipulation of network
resources without costly and cumbersome server reconfiguration. Users
have access to all of their files--and only those that they are
permitted to see--in a user-friendly, Windows/DOS style file
management environment, even with non-Windows servers!

This system interface increases security as user access is possible
only through server authenticated logins and passwords.  Unauthorized
users do not see, therefore, cannot access, the drives for which they 
have no permissions. 

MPAS is available at a price your institution can afford. For a  
limited time you can purchase MPAS at a special introductory price 
of $10 per client with a minimum 20 seat purchase.  For more
information, or a 30 day free trial, visit the MPAS web site at
http://www.mpas.com, e-mail Strategic Forecasting at info@mpas.com 
or call 504-267-5507.




