Hi,

This post is to announce a new, improved port of the WISE project 
management and metrics package to the Linux operating system.

Changes:

 *) More bug fixes.

 *) This version now requires mSQL version 2.0.  

 *) A new report generation mechanism has been added in order
    to gracefully support large project databases.  In the older 
    versions, a list of more than a few hundred defects was
    difficult to scan through.
 
 *) gnuplot a.out binaries removed.


This package can be retreived from
http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/wise-1.0c.tar.gz
and
http://linas.org/linux/wise/wise-1.0c.tar.gz
it should shortly appear in
http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/devel/vc/wise-1.0c.tar.gz

The LSM below provides additional details; the original
WISE web site at
http://research.ivv.nasa.gov/projects/WISE/wise.html
provides a nice overview and demo of the package.

- --linas

P.S. I am looking for volunteers to add templates for other 
project types, e.g. software architecture, proposal tracking,
help-desk operations, release management, to name a few.

I am also looking for volunteers to add a (Visual) Tcl 
interface for the project description language so that
it becomes easier to manage team membership lists, create
new project templates, etc.

- --linas


