SVCS Linux SIG					Wednesday, May 7, 7pm


		GNU Utilities for Windows 95/NT
		-------------------------------

Most PCs today are not running Linux, so the next best thing is getting the
Linux (GNU) utilities on top of Windows. The May meeting will be a
presentation on the GNU-Win32 Project from Cygnus Solutions.

The Cygwin32 library provides a POSIX-like layer that makes it easy to port
many complex Unix programs to Windows 95 and NT. Using this technology,
Cygnus has ported many of the popular GNU tools to Win32. Together, the
freely distributed GNU-Win32 tools provide a Unix-like development/user
environment that thousands of people are now using.

Geoffrey Noer is the chief engineer of the Cygwin32 API layer at Cygnus
Solutions. In addition to making his own technical contributions, he
coordinates the development efforts of Internet contributors, manages the
GNU-Win32 public releases, and tries to maintain an active presence on the
project mailing lists. The upcoming beta 18 release will be his third since
he took over the project in June, 1996.

Cygnus Solutions is a software development tools company focused on
addressing the challenges of supporting multiple platforms from a single
source base.


