We are pleased to announce the immediate availability of our Vprint Text
Formatter. Vprint is a Troff-like formatter (it used both command line
and embedded commands for formatting), however it is NOT troff
compatible.

Vprint is feature rich, supports just about any printer, is compact, and
easy to learn. It was originally written for OS9 operating systems, and
has now been ported to the Linux platform.

The 200K archive contains the executables, a full manual, other docs,
sample files, etc. It can be downloaded from my web site
<http://www2.awinc.com/users/bvdpoel>.

This is NOT FREEWARE. You will be granted a licence to use the software
without charge. More verbage and a features list are on the web
site...have a look. Comments welcome.


