S.u.S.E. Opens New California Office 
S.u.S.E. Linux 4.4.1 Now Available in Full English Version
==========================================================

OAKLAND, CA. (April 28, 1997) -- Germany's market-leading Linux
publisher, S.u.S.E., GmbH of Fuerth, opened its new U.S. affiliate
here today, S.u.S.E., LLC. 

Recently, S.u.S.E. published an English version of it's Linux 
distribution, currently Version 4.4.1 (kernel 2.0.29) which means 
that many more users have access to S.u.S.E.'s contributions to 
Linux that the Germans have enjoyed for years, such as the versatile
YaST setup tool, excellent memory management capabilities, punctual 
updates and excellent technical support. 

The product consists of 3 CD-ROMs and a 420-page reference book.
Included is YaST, short for "Yet another Setup Tool" which affords 
users of all levels maximum flexibility and efficiency in installing
and configuring Linux. For Linux veterans YaST satisfies the need 
for maximum system control and fine-tuning.  For example, a sidebar 
gives real-time information about available disk space, which 
pre-empts memory exhaustion and saves time. At the same time YaST 
fulfills the beginner's requirement for effortless installation 
and configuration. Ready-to-run pre-configuration scripts for the 
sample user are included, as well as a warning system which warns
against deletion of vital system components. 

Price: $49.95

You can find out more at:

