- -Reader Response, Packaging Formats & Responsibility of Linux Advocates 
 
The following was in response to the article "So, which 'Linux Distribution' 
or 'CD' is the best anyway? where I spoke about creating a Linux 
Distribution Comparison document in Linux Newsletter #4 (available at 
http://www.LinuxMall.com/announce/lxnews.004.txt). 
 
I think that there are several issues in this email exchange between Chuck 
and myself that Linux Advocates need to be aware of.  Linux Packaging 
needs to become standardized, and UN-installs need to be able to restore 
what was in place before the install occurred in case of a problem.  Even 
Debian & RH have not done this yet. Dependencies problems need not 
just to be reported, but the choice must be given to resolve them.
 
In addition I often hear: "I am just the tech, and I work with 
whatever management tells me to work with."  But things are changing 
as management and employees in high technology companies learn how to 
listen to each other better.  
 
