Title:          This is mbiff-0.1
File:           mbiff-0.1.readme
Date:           Mon May  5 18:31:44 MET DST 1997
Required:       X11, qt-1.2, pine, [procmail]
Comment:        A multiple INBOX biff.
Comment2:       Does launch/monitor mailreader for multiple inboxes.
Author:         Michael Leodolter
Email:          Michael.Leodolter@univie.ac.at
Install:        Adapt Makefile to your system.
Install2:       Run make and install mbiff as /usr/local/bin/mbiff.
Install3:       See below for procmail/fvwm95 hints.
How to Get:    
<ftp://lab1.psy.univie.ac.at/pub/qt/mbiff/mbiff-0.1.tar.gz>
Missing:        No config options yet.

What is mbiff:
- --------------

Mbiff is biff program for multiple INBOX'es under Linux/Unix+X11.
I just took the biff examples from qt-1.2 sources 
and did some more and got this.


How does it work:
- -----------------

With mbiff you get a window with one line per INBOX + 
real INBOX as first line.
Each line showing the biff-icon + 3 numbers:

        ----------------------
        |  BI userid 1 2 17  |
        |  BI qt 0 66 83     |
        |  BI dosemu 0 19 25 |
        ----------------------

The first number is the number of new messages since INBOX was last
read.
The second number is the number of unread messages in the INBOX.
The second number is the number of messages in the INBOX.

If the INBOX folder's name is 'INBOX-qt' only 'qt' is displayed.

How I have installed mbiff for fvwm95:
- --------------------------------------

#========================================================================#
# File:         .fvwm2rc95
#========================================================================#
#
# Set the decoration styles and window options
#
Style "mbiff"        NoTitle,            Sticky, WindowListSkip
#
#------------------ FvwmButtons
*FvwmButtons(Title mbiff, Icon Mail.xpm, \
                Action 'Exec "mbiff" /usr/local/bin/mbiff \
                INBOX-qt INBOX-dosemu INBOX-djgpp &')

How I have installed procmail:

#========================================================================#
# File:         .forward
#========================================================================#
"|IFS=' '&&exec /usr/bin/procmail -f-||exit 75 #YOUR_USERNAME"

#========================================================================#
# File:         .procmailrc
#========================================================================#
MAILDIR=$HOME/mail
LOGFILE=$MAILDIR/procmail.log

# backup all mail to $MAILDIR/mail-backup
#:0 c
#mail-backup

:0:
* (^To|^Cc|^Subject).*qt
INBOX-qt

:0:
* (^To|^Cc|^Subject).*dosemu
INBOX-dosemu

:0:
* (^To|^Cc|^Subject).*djgpp
INBOX-djgpp
#========================================================================#

Good luck,

	michael
