In need of a new utility to mirror or lurk around FTP sites?  Look no
further..

Announcing the availability of:

lurkftp v0.95 ("bugfree")

What it is: This is the ultimate ftp site lurker program.  It is a simple
program to monitor changes in ftp sites and either just report changes or
mirror changes into a local directory.

It has undergone only a few real changes & enhancements since v0.91, but
here's a summary of current features:

 - Recursively retrieves directory either with single command or via manual
   recursion, or retrieves remote ls-lR file (and optionally uncompresses it),
   or uses self-generated placemarker file as pseudo-remote site.

 - Compares remote directory with either a placemarker file or actual contents
   of local directory.

 - Optionally generates a report; optionally generates a placemarker file;
   optionally retrieves new files and either places them in the local
   directory or pipes them to a command.

Some other nifty features are FTP timeout+retry (of course), include/exclude
regular expression filters (of course), detection of moved files, file-retry
with automatic use of restart (append) mode (instead of starting over @
start), automatic mailing of reports to users (or not if no report is
generated), relatively free-format option files (with ~, ${env_var}, ', and
" handling), relatively small binary (52K on my system), and use of fork() to
process multiple sites in parallel.  The man page is relatively accurate &
complete, so read that & the README included in the archive for details.

This is probably the last, great, "stable" release before I go & totally
rewrite it again.

