What is CasioBoss?
- ------------------
It is a package originally ported from DOS to allow communication to
the CASIO series of hand-held organizers based on a protocol posted
by Knut Radloff <knut@krhh.hanse.de>. There has been substantial
change from the DOS origins.
Version 2.1 has been tested on Linux2.x , Solaris2.x, sunos4.x.
It is provided as is i.e. i am not to be responsible for any
damages it causes to you, your CASIO or your environment.

Whats new in 2.1?
- ----------------
   2.1     22 Feb 1996  Birko Bergt(Birko.Bergt@cdc.com)     Added config
           file (.casiorc) and commandline overiding of the config file.
   2.1     30 Apr 1996  J. Hadi Salim (hadi@cyberus.ca)  Added support for
           different parity,speeds etc + recognition of more data types


the lsm:
- --------

